{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And the Avvim who dwelt in Chatzerim, etc.</b> The Avvim are of the Philistines — for with them they are reckoned in the book of Joshua, as it says (Joshua 13): ״חֲמֵשֶׁת סַרְנֵי פְלִשְׁתִּים הָעַזָּתִי וְהָאַשְׁדּוֹדִי הָאֶשְׁקְלוֹנִי הַגִּתִּי וְהָעֶקְרוֹנִי וְהָעַוִּים״. And because of the oath that Abraham swore to Avimelech, Israel could not take their land from them, so I brought the Caphtorim upon them and they destroyed them and dwelt in their stead — and now you are permitted to take it from their hand (Chulin 60a)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:45:43.607320510Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}